# {{.Name}}

A goowee app: a Go UI compiled to WebAssembly.

## Layout

- `app/`: the whole UI, package `app`. It builds on the host, so
  `go test ./...` runs its gooweetest tests without a browser.
- `main.go`: the browser entry point (`//go:build js && wasm`).
- `web/`: static files; `index.html` is the page shell.
{{- if .SSR}}
- `server/`: the server. It renders pages with `ssr.Handler` and serves the
  static files.
{{- end}}

## Commands

- `goowee dev`: build, serve on http://localhost:8080, and rebuild and
  reload the page on every change. Build errors show in the page.
- `go test ./...`: the tests.
- `goowee build`: a production build in `dist/`, with a size report.

(`goowee` is `go run github.com/yogisalomo/goowee/cmd/goowee`.)

## Rules

- Components are `core.Component` functions; state is `hooks.UseState`.
- Bind changing values (`TextS`, `ClassS`, `BindAttr`) rather than reading
  signals in render code; `go vet -vettool=$(which gooweevet)` checks it.
- Format with `strconv` and `TextS` rather than `fmt`/`Textf` where size
  matters: fmt adds about 35 KB brotli to the WASM.
